  {
   "start": 182.36,
   "end": 192.36,
   "text": "Legally it's impossible. Legally it's impossible. Legalement c'est impossible."
  },
  {
   "start": 192.36,
   "end": 200.36,
   "text": "Legalement c'est impossible. C'est impossible. If you want to say it's impossible to do"
  },
  {
   "start": 200.36,
   "end": 206.36,
   "text": "it, you will say in French, it is impossible of to do it. So what was the word for of"
  },
  {
   "start": 206.36,
   "end": 216.36,
   "text": "from? De. De. And to do? Faire. Faire. So it is impossible to do it."
  },
  {
   "start": 216.36,
   "end": 224.64,
   "text": "It is impossible of to do it. C'est impossible de faire. And it?"
  },
  {
   "start": 224.64,
   "end": 233.64,
   "text": "De le faire? Good. C'est impossible de le faire. C'est impossible de le faire."
  },
  {
   "start": 233.64,
   "end": 241.64,
   "text": "And this de le doesn't contract to do, no. Like when we say of the something."
  },
  {
   "start": 241.64,
   "end": 249.64,
   "text": "And this is because they're not connected in meaning, no. We have of to do it rather than of the."
  },
  {
   "start": 249.64,
   "end": 257.64,
   "text": "So these meanings are separated. So liaisons as well as contractions like de le to do"
  },
  {
   "start": 257.64,
   "end": 261.64,
   "text": "only happen with words that are so connected in meaning that the language"
  },
  {
   "start": 261.64,
   "end": 268.64,
   "text": "is happy with making them one word. Ce soir, ce soir, means tonight or this evening."
  },
  {
   "start": 268.64,
   "end": 276.64,
   "text": "Ce soir. Ce soir. Ce soir. You will hear a ce soir in French like see you tonight, no."
  },
  {
   "start": 276.64,
   "end": 281.64,
   "text": "A ce soir and to tonight. So we have ce soir this evening tonight."
  },
  {
   "start": 281.64,
   "end": 286.64,
   "text": "How would you say is it possible to do it tonight, this evening?"
  },
  {
   "start": 287.64,
   "end": 297.64,
   "text": "C'est possible de le faire ce soir."
  },
  {
   "start": 297.64,
   "end": 305.64,
   "text": "I do in French is je fais. That's spelled F-A-I-S."
  },
  {
   "start": 305.64,
   "end": 312.64,
   "text": "And of course we have the A-I giving us an E sound like in maison. How would you say I'm not doing it?"
  },
  {
   "start": 314.95,
   "end": 324.95,
   "text": "Je ne le fais pas. I'm not doing anything tonight. I'm not doing anything this evening."
  },
  {
   "start": 326.95,
   "end": 338.95,
   "text": "Je ne fais rien ce soir. So we have je fais, no, F-A-I-S. And you do is tu fais."
  },
  {
   "start": 338.95,
   "end": 347.95,
   "text": "It's spelled the same F-A-I-S. Tu fais. How was the word for but? The word for but it also ended A-I-S."
  },
  {
   "start": 347.95,
   "end": 359.95,
   "text": "Mais. Mais. Good. M-A-I-S. But mais. Jamais. Jamais. J-A-M-A-I-S is never. Jamais."
  },
  {
   "start": 359.95,
   "end": 370.95,
   "text": "And this also combines with ne to give us a negation in French. And never in English actually is also just ne and ever combining."
  },
  {
   "start": 370.95,
   "end": 379.95,
   "text": "So ne and jamais combine to give us the meaning of never, not ever. So how would you say you never do it? You never do it."
  },
  {
   "start": 380.95,
   "end": 386.95,
   "text": "Tu ne le fais jamais."
  },
  {
   "start": 386.95,
   "end": 397.95,
   "text": "And we can combine jamais and rien to get the meaning of never anything. You never do anything. We can combine jamais and rien."
  },
  {
   "start": 397.95,
   "end": 402.95,
   "text": "So jamais, rien, never anything. How would that be? You never do anything."
  },
  {
   "start": 403.95,
   "end": 405.95,
   "text": "Tu ne fais jamais."
  },
  {
   "start": 405.95,
   "end": 415.95,
   "text": "Try to think 100% just on the bit you're dealing with now. Because when your mind is thinking about how you're going to make jamais, rien, or how you'll pronounce something later,"
  },
  {
   "start": 415.95,
   "end": 423.95,
   "text": "then the stuff you're pronouncing at the moment, we tend to go back to making the same mistakes we were making before that we've, you know, made a little effort to stop doing."
  },
  {
   "start": 423.95,
   "end": 427.95,
   "text": "So think about one bit at a time. You never do anything."
  },
  {
   "start": 428.95,
   "end": 433.95,
   "text": "Tu ne, tu ne fais jamais rien."
  },
  {
   "start": 433.95,
   "end": 436.95,
   "text": "Tu ne fais jamais rien."
  },
  {
   "start": 436.95,
   "end": 444.95,
   "text": "So it's much better that you insist with yourself, you know, to take yourself through it slowly and focus 100% on, OK, do I have the right E sound?"
  },
  {
   "start": 444.95,
   "end": 451.95,
   "text": "You know, et cetera, all the questions you might have to focus on those for each bit and go slowly."
  },
  {
   "start": 451.95,
   "end": 454.95,
   "text": "Tu ne fais jamais rien."
  },
  {
   "start": 454.95,
   "end": 456.95,
   "text": "What was to eat?"
